  "id": "COMPOUND:25971 - PROTEIN:6231",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between (+)-Phylliroside and Histone-lysine N-methyltransferase, H3 lysine-9 specific 5, through a series of molecular interactions. (+)-Phylliroside is identified as a target of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which is itself a target of quillaic acid alpha-L-Arap-(1->4)-alpha-L-Arap-(1->3)-beta-D-Xylp-(1->4)-alpha-L-Rhap-(1->2)-beta-D-fucopyranosyl ester, and also of Dimethyl 3-hydroxyphthalate. Both quillaic acid and Dimethyl 3-hydroxyphthalate are known to interact with the histone methyltransferase complex, which is responsible for modifying histone lysine residues, particularly lysine 9 of histone H3. This suggests that (+)-Phylliroside may exert its biological effects through a pathway involving the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which in turn modulates the activity of the histone methyltransferase. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between (+)-Phylliroside and the target enzyme, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
